abstract: >-
  Zero-dependency Node.js ESM, Python 3, and WebGL 2.0 multi-scale Artificial Life
  observatory supervising eight local endpoints across seven public repositories on
  127.0.0.1:8790. The displayed T1/T2-to-T3/T4 coupling cells are fixed at D7RO with
  strength 0; no code path writing T1/T2 data into Asmodensius was found by inspection,
  but no automated test checks this. Automated example-based and seeded-random tests
  cover loopback CSRF/CSWSH request predicates, path-traversal rejection, 1..1,000,000
  population clamping (compared between Node and Python on normalized inputs), 112-trait
  spectral differentials and a <=240-sample history ring; 6/6 hand-planted regression
  mutants in lib/observatory_core.mjs are killed. These are tests, not proofs; the
  repository contains no Lean code. It is a visualization and orchestration instrument
  and retires 0/1,900 Mega-Atlas open problems.
